{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe underestimation of volatility: The model consistently fails to capture sudden upward spikes (e.g., 70.52 to 76.67), predicting flat or slightly declining paths instead. Apply a volatility multiplier or spike-detection trigger to forecast adjustments when recent history shows a sharp upward trend.",
    "Adjust for excessive mean reversion bias: Forecasts revert to a narrow mean (~70-71) too quickly after price spikes, ignoring the persistence of elevated levels. Extend the decay rate of the mean reversion parameter to allow prices to stay higher for longer after a breakout.",
    "Invert sentiment weighting for short-term horizons: High sentiment scores (1.00) in the history often precede immediate price drops or stagnation in the model's output, suggesting the model overreacts to positive sentiment as a signal for immediate gains rather than a lagging indicator. Reduce the weight of immediate positive sentiment on the first 5-10 days of the forecast.",
    "Apply a downward correction for long-horizon forecasts: The model systematically overestimates prices beyond day 15-20, failing to account for the eventual sharp decline seen in true outcomes. Apply a negative drift correction to the tail end of the 30-day forecast horizon.",
    "Lag adjustment for trend reversal: The model lags significantly in identifying trend reversals from bull to bear markets. Introduce a momentum reversal filter that triggers a downward adjustment when the 5-day moving average crosses below the 10-day moving average, regardless of sentiment score."
  ]
}
